WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.949 --> 00:00:05.769
Every year,

00:00:05.780 --> 00:00:09.180
Russia puts its military might on display on Victory day,

00:00:09.189 --> 00:00:12.720
celebrating the Soviet Union's victory over Nazi Germany.

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:28.420
The choreographed spectacle is also a chance for Moscow to showcase its latest 

00:00:28.430 --> 00:00:31.889
weapons to potential foreign buyers with weaponry.

00:00:31.899 --> 00:00:33.740
It's not just lucrative to export it,

00:00:33.750 --> 00:00:37.700
but it was also important as a sort of geopolitical outreach for Russia.

00:00:38.759 --> 00:00:42.880
But the country's share of the global weapons trade has been dropping since 

00:00:42.889 --> 00:00:44.130
2017,

00:00:44.180 --> 00:00:47.119
from 22% to 16%.

00:00:47.799 --> 00:00:52.720
And images of destroyed Russian weapons across Ukraine have dented the reputation 

00:00:52.729 --> 00:00:54.099
of its arms industry.

00:00:54.520 --> 00:00:59.250
So here is why Russia's position as the world's second largest weapons exporter is 

00:00:59.259 --> 00:01:00.209
under threat.

00:01:04.029 --> 00:01:08.809
Problems began in 2014 when Russia annexed Crimea from Ukraine.

00:01:09.129 --> 00:01:13.930
This led to sanctions that limited the flow of Western components that are crucial in 

00:01:13.940 --> 00:01:15.419
some Russian weapons.

00:01:16.849 --> 00:01:21.220
And last year's invasion of Ukraine triggered more economic sanctions and more 

00:01:21.230 --> 00:01:22.720
complications for the Kremlin.

00:01:23.400 --> 00:01:28.080
Not only has it become harder for countries to buy Russian arms and components,

00:01:28.110 --> 00:01:30.010
it's also more difficult to pay for them.

00:01:30.019 --> 00:01:30.529
Now,

00:01:31.059 --> 00:01:32.349
if you're paying in the dollar,

00:01:32.360 --> 00:01:33.010
for instance,

00:01:33.019 --> 00:01:37.970
the US can sanction you for doing that And so a good example of that is the Philippines 

00:01:37.980 --> 00:01:41.129
canceled an order of Russian helicopters precisely because of that.

00:01:42.199 --> 00:01:46.690
Russia's problems are creating opportunities for competitors like France,

00:01:47.279 --> 00:01:48.180
Serbia,

00:01:48.190 --> 00:01:52.489
an ally of Moscow is in talks to buy French Rafa fighter jets.

00:01:55.160 --> 00:01:59.970
Another issue is Russia's own need for weapons as it offensive in Ukraine drags 

00:01:59.980 --> 00:02:04.489
on Russia has likely lost more than 2000 tanks in 

00:02:04.500 --> 00:02:05.269
Ukraine.

00:02:05.589 --> 00:02:08.000
That's more than half its operational fleet.

00:02:08.009 --> 00:02:09.479
According to one estimate,

00:02:10.679 --> 00:02:15.130
this raises questions about how many weapons Moscow has left for export.

00:02:16.039 --> 00:02:17.529
Russia's biggest arms buyer.

00:02:17.539 --> 00:02:22.089
India said in March that a major delivery from Moscow wasn't going to take 

00:02:22.100 --> 00:02:24.179
place because of the Ukraine War,

00:02:24.539 --> 00:02:25.179
China.

00:02:25.190 --> 00:02:29.350
The next biggest customer has also become less reliant on Russian made 

00:02:29.360 --> 00:02:30.220
weapons.

00:02:30.229 --> 00:02:34.800
Countries like India and China are very important and are likely harbinger of 

00:02:34.809 --> 00:02:39.660
much worse to come for the Russian arms industry because they are starting to make more of their own weaponry.

00:02:40.259 --> 00:02:45.149
Some analysts say Russia's performance on the battlefield could further weaken demand for 

00:02:45.160 --> 00:02:46.029
its equipment.

00:02:46.660 --> 00:02:49.190
Some people would argue that it's not so much Russian equipment,

00:02:49.199 --> 00:02:49.649
that's bad.

00:02:49.660 --> 00:02:52.550
It's the tactics and the people who are using it.

00:02:52.779 --> 00:02:55.199
The Ukrainians have used some Russian armor for instance,

00:02:55.210 --> 00:02:56.750
its tanks to great effect,

00:02:57.020 --> 00:02:59.729
but a lot of people would say that it's very damaging for Russia.

00:03:00.029 --> 00:03:04.649
Russia didn't immediately respond to a request for comment on the decline of its 

00:03:04.660 --> 00:03:06.330
global arms exports.

00:03:08.410 --> 00:03:13.300
These difficulties are likely to further reduce Moscow's share of the global weapons 

00:03:13.309 --> 00:03:14.059
trade.

00:03:14.460 --> 00:03:18.630
Its arms exports dropped 31% in the five years that ended in 

00:03:18.639 --> 00:03:23.139
2022 compared with the same period ending in 2017.

00:03:23.490 --> 00:03:28.100
That's according to a report by the Stockholm International Peace Research Institute,

00:03:28.830 --> 00:03:33.419
the think tank uses multi year periods because yearly figures can be distorted by 

00:03:33.429 --> 00:03:34.759
large deliveries.

00:03:37.830 --> 00:03:42.429
It's very hard to say and therefore Russia will continue to fade as a major arms 

00:03:42.440 --> 00:03:43.139
exporter.

00:03:43.149 --> 00:03:47.929
But it's problematic on so many different fronts for the Russian's arm industry that there are obvious 

00:03:47.940 --> 00:03:50.750
reasons why if you were in the Russian arm industry,

00:03:50.759 --> 00:03:51.949
you would fear its future.

